KZ2 patch 6100 (2026-11-25; follows up the review of patch 6094): the indirect-call
guards and diagnostics name the dispatched target, not CTR. Since patch 6094 the target travels as the argument `addr`
of ps3_indirect_call_impl_at / ps3_indirect_call_entry: CTR for ps3_indirect_call, but LR for ps3_indirect_call_to
(b<cond>lrl; CTR is the guest's and unrelated), and opd[0] after PPU_OPD_RECOVER. The garbage-vcall no-op, the stuck-loop
guard, the unresolved-call log, the 0x39800000 import-stub check, PS3_ICALL_GATE's histogram, PPU_CSCHECK's target and
the BCTRL_RING / PS3_BREADCRUMB records read ctx->ctr, so for ps3_indirect_call_to they judged the wrong address (a
valid target could be no-op'd as garbage, or a garbage one dispatched). All now read addr. For ps3_indirect_call the
two are equal, so nothing changes there. PPU_TOCWATCH's "ctr=" field still prints CTR (it is labelled so).
Host tests: tools/runtime/test_ppu_icall_to.sh and test_ppu_icall_diag.sh pass on the patched tree; neither reaches
the guard code (it sits after the 6094 "dispatch core" block the first one compiles), so no case covers the change
itself yet (a case would need that block marked out too).

